<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haryana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haryana is a state of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> surrounding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> on three sides, with Chandigarh, shared with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, as its capital. The region includes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a> and Panipat, scenes of famous battles, and lay at the heart of ancient and medieval north Indian states. It was carved out of the Indian state of Punjab in 1966 as a mainly Hindi-speaking state and is among the most prosperous in India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haryana.jpg" alt="Haryana" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tarun4u · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cyber_City_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
